55
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:25,400
But what you find
out actually is

56
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,185
that m is going to equal 7.

57
00:02:27,185 --> 00:02:30,210
The reason is we're

58
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:33,540
evaluating that ++ expression

59
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,940
twice on a macro substitution.

60
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:38,380
We're evaluating it once in

61
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:41,360
the condition check and
once in the return value.

62
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,760
Based again on the
fact that we're

63
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,260
just directly replacing a,

64
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:47,180
with everything that we're
typing into the min macro.

65
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:50,440
This can result in some
unexpected and difficult to

66
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:52,330
